    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "The linear contrasts $ y^* $ are equivalent to residual deviations from the estimated fixed effects, akin to using $ y_i^* = y_i - \\overline{y} $ in the introductory example used at the start of this chapter. REML estimates of variance components are equivalent to ML estimates of the transformed variables. Thus, we can use the ML solutions outlined above by making the following substitutions:",
